      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "しゃがむ describes lowering oneself into a squatting position with both feet flat on the ground. This is a common posture in Japanese culture, often used when resting, working at ground level, or waiting.\n\nCONJUGATION (godan verb):\n- しゃがむ (dictionary form)\n- しゃがまない (negative)\n- しゃがんだ (past)\n- しゃがんで (te-form)\n\nRELATED EXPRESSIONS:\n- しゃがみ{込|こ}む: to squat down and stay (more prolonged action)",
